-# M1 fixture · Legacy-Style Host Plugin (0.1.1-rc.2 Era)
+# M1 fixture · Host Plugin (migrated from the 0.1.1-rc.2 era)
 
 Test fixture, **do not publish**. The content is copied verbatim from the `/tmp/demo-plugin` of the historical validation environment (legacy style written against the real interface of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy@0.0.1-rc.1`); the only additions are `"private": true` in package.json and this README.
 
 Activation facts (from `benchmark/results/validation-report-2026-08-30.md`):
 
-- With this plugin attached, dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cold boot immediately fails with `plugin tree failed ... pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)` and exit 1;
+- With the legacy plugin attached, dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cold boot immediately fails with `plugin tree failed ... pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)` and exit 1;
 - After migrating per the skill card (`inject: ["llm"]` + `ctx.llm.listProviders()` + removing the dead dependency), activation succeeds; with no API key in the container, a route count of 0 is expected — as long as the calls go through.
+
+## Migration status
+
+Migrated in place against `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`:
+
+- `index.js` injects `["llm"]` and lists providers with `ctx.llm.listProviders()` (the successor of `apiProxy.llm.providers`; `LlmRuntime` owns provider facts and exposes `llm/listProviders` as a Remote);
+- the dead `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy` dependency was removed from `package.json`;
+- `cordis.patch.yml` — the `dsh.bundle.patch` layer that inserts the `upgrade-demo` row — is unchanged and still matches the current bundle format.
+
+Verified: the headless boot probe (`--profile probe ping` against a dead model endpoint) activates the plugin and reaches the model call instead of hanging on `pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)`.
